Approach Guarantee Failure modes Free text + regex/parse None Prose around JSON, format drift, locale formats JSON mode Syntactically valid JSON Wrong keys/types, missing fields Structured Outputs (JSON Schema, constrained decoding) Output conforms to the schema Semantically wrong values, refusals, truncation (<code>finish_reason=length</code>), schema features unsupported by the provider <p>In MEAI, <code>GetResponseAsync&lt;T&gt;()</code> derives a JSON schema from your C# type and asks the provider for schema-constrained output where supported (falling back to prompt-described JSON otherwise — verify the <code>useJsonSchemaResponseFormat</code> parameter and fallback behavior in your MEAI version):</p> <pre><code>ChatResponse&lt;IncidentReport&gt; r = await chat.GetResponseAsync&lt;IncidentReport&gt;(
    messages, options, useJsonSchemaResponseFormat: true, cancellationToken: ct);  // verify signature
if (!r.TryGetResult(out IncidentReport? report))
    return ExtractionResult.Failed(r.FinishReason, r.Text);
</code></pre> <p>Design rules for output types:</p> <ul> <li>Make unknown representable: nullable fields, an explicit <code>Unknown</code> enum member, and a <code>MissingInformation</code> list. A non-nullable <code>bool InjuriesReported</code> forces the model to guess.</li> <li>Enums over free strings for categories; <code>[Description]</code> attributes on types and properties become schema descriptions the model reads.</li> <li>Strict-mode constraints (provider-specific): typically all properties required, <code>additionalProperties: false</code>, nullability via <code>["type","null"]</code>; some keywords unsupported. Keep schemas flat and small; deep nesting raises failure rates and token cost.</li> <li>Validate anyway: schema-valid ≠ correct. Run business validation (plate exists? date not in the future? km within road length?) and route failures to a human or a repair prompt.</li> <li>Not universal: Azure's catalog lists several models without tool calling or with text-only formats; local SLMs are weaker at schema adherence (your C0 Lab 4 count). Check per deployment.</li> </ul>
